      <h2>Why Beating the Kick-Off Price Matters More Than Any Single Match Result</h2>
      <p>The <strong>Closing Line</strong> is the final odds available right at kick-off (e.g., Saturday 4:00 PM WAT for the Premier League) after all team news, weather, and sharp syndicate money have been priced into the global market.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Suppose on Thursday you back <strong>Bayer Leverkusen -0.5 @ 2.05</strong>. By Saturday kick-off, after confirmed lineups show Victor Boniface and Florian Wirtz starting while the opponent''s key centre-back is out, the price has dropped to <strong>1.78</strong>.</li>
        <li>Even if Leverkusen hits the woodwork three times and draws 1–1 on the day, your process was <strong>mathematically profitable</strong> because you bought an asset worth <code>1.78</code> at a price of <code>2.05</code>. Track your CLV across 50+ bets in PunterStat to verify your true analytical edge.</li>
      </ul>

<h2>Real-Data Benchmark: PunterStat v2.0 Model Calibration vs Market</h2>
